{
  "id": "9f1e2d3c-4b5a-6789-8abc-def012345678",
  "name": "Personal AI Agent",
  "active": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Personal AI Agent\n\nPowered by OpenRouter (multi-provider LLM).\n\n**Tools wired in:**\n- remember_memory / search_memory \u2014 persistent memory via agentmemory REST (localhost:3111)\n- list_skills / run_skill \u2014 skill packs from the skills service\n- get_profile \u2014 the user's personal profile database (job applications)\n- browse_web \u2014 real browser automation via browser-use sidecar\n\n**Chat:** built-in chat UI (Open chat) or POST {\"message\": \"...\"} to /webhook/agent.\n\n**Setup after import:** select your OpenRouter credential in the Chat Model node.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 360
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -380,
        -60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "agent",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Agent Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -160,
        220
      ],
      "webhookId": "agent-webhook"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "When chat message received",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chatTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        -160,
        -40
      ],
      "webhookId": "agent-chat"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.chatInput ?? $json.body?.message ?? $json.message }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "={{ \"Current date: \" + $now.toFormat(\"yyyy-MM-dd (cccc)\") + \"\\n\\n\" + ($json.soul ? $json.soul + \"\\n\\n\" : \"\") + \"You are a capable personal AI agent running on n8n.\\n\\n# Operating protocol\\n1. MEMORY FIRST: At the start of a task, call search_memory for relevant stored knowledge about the user and prior work. Use what you find; never ask what the user already told you before.\\n2.5 DOCUMENTS: The user's document folder (resumes, certificates, cover letters, notes \u2014 .txt/.md/.pdf/.docx/.doc) is accessible via search_docs (keyword search; full_doc=true returns whole documents) and read_docs (full text of one document, or name='all' for EVERY document). When the user asks you to read their folder/all documents/database, call read_docs with name='all'. For experience, skills, or certificate questions, call search_docs first and cite the source file name. For CURRENT role, timeline, or education-order questions, use search_docs with full_doc=true and read the complete document before answering \u2014 snippets alone can mislead about which job is current.\\n2. SKILLS: For tasks matching an available skill (see list_skills), call run_skill with the skill name and the user's request, then follow the returned instructions to produce your answer. If unsure which skill applies, call list_skills first.\\n3. PROFILE: For resumes, CVs, cover letters, job applications, or ANY question about the user's background (experience, education, skills, contact info), call get_profile first and use only facts from it.\\n4. BROWSER: For anything requiring live web pages, browsing, or form interaction, use the browse_web tool with a clear, self-contained task description.\\n5. MEMORY LAST: When the user shares durable preferences, facts, or you complete a non-trivial task, store a concise note with remember_memory.\\n6. If a tool fails, say so plainly, then answer from your own knowledge with a caveat.\\n\\n# Style\\n- Be direct and concise. Lead with the answer, then supporting detail.\\n- Use markdown formatting and code blocks where appropriate.\" }}"
        }
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "AI Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        240,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "openrouter/free",
          "mode": "list"
        },
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.4
        }
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "LLM (via LiteLLM proxy)",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        60,
        340
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "b8d4f2a1-5678-4abc-9def-0123456789cd",
          "name": "LiteLLM Proxy (OpenRouter+Gemini+Groq)"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "sessionIdType": "customKey",
        "sessionKey": "={{ $json.sessionId ?? $json.body?.sessionId ?? 'cli' }}",
        "contextWindowLength": 10,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0000-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "name": "Session Memory",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.memoryBufferWindow",
